## Start gate

Required completed exports: [Geometric assembly and joint relations](Relations.lingua); [Simplification and safe support products](Simplification.lingua); [Supplied character appearance and navigation](Character-Starter.lingua)

Dependency reason: Editable rigs require shared geometric relations and source/LOD correspondence first. Exact CAD and geography remain separate consumers.

This is a core work package. Start only after the named providers publish verified native/backend/persistence contracts and the package's implementation scope is authorized. Do not wait for an entire former numbered stage unless that contract acceptance is explicitly listed above. Do not use an unfinished sibling or mocked replacement as a hidden prerequisite.

## Delivered boundary

Rig/link/control editing, forward/limited inverse posing, source-to-bind repair, skins/morphs/attachments and native undo/export.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Rig/deformation evaluator and character-native tools; no independent relation/save/query system.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 11.T06

- [ ] **11.T06.** Extend the shared assembly/constraint model with stable articulated links/ports, reference configurations, typed joint coordinates/limits/couplings and rig/control-to-source maps. Provide joint/control creation, numeric forward posing, bounded endpoint/constraint solving, reference/pose editing and supported rest/bind updates through the same commands/history/undo/selection. Solve dirty connected regions with explicit residual/limit/unreachable/ambiguous status; a cyclic mechanism is not silently forced into a human bone tree. Preserve source frames/units, occurrence-local state and a recoverable accepted pose on failed/stale/cancelled solving.

### Task 11.T07

- [ ] **11.T07.** Implement the selected skinning, authored morph/corrective and attachment subsets with versioned source bindings, ordinary weight/region/parameter tools and native previews. Validate joint indices, finite/nonnegative normalized weights, bind transforms, topology revision, transform conventions and admitted influence counts. Shape edits invalidate/rebuild only affected bindings/products; retain the old valid result until replacement or explicit repair. Extend the declared import/export subset for rig/skin/morph/clip data and semantic maps, preserving source/licensing/unsupported fields. Reuse stage 08's simplification and source/correspondence lifecycle for pose-tested low-poly variants.

